&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Building demanding products on Open Source foundations for decades&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Open Source advocate and notable author since the 1990s, e.g. I wrote &lt;code&gt;unittest.py&lt;/code&gt; for the Python standard library around 2000&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Contributed to &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/purcell?tab=repositories&quot;&gt;many hundreds (!) of repositories&lt;/a&gt; in various languages&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Was in the top 100 most active GitHub developers worldwide for several years&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Largely built up an &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/melpa/melpa&quot;&gt;open source community project&lt;/a&gt; from an early prototype to having thousands of contributors and 0.3B downloads&lt;/li&gt; 
